WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.268
-My next guest
is a talented actor,

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.837
who stars
in "The Suicide Squad,"

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:08.474
which is in theaters
and streaming now on HBO Max.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:12.745
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Jai Courtney!

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:16.482
-♪ Jai Courtney
makes the crowd applaud ♪

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:20.553
♪ For his new movie,
"The Suicide Squad" ♪

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:24.523
♪ You know he rides with
the DC Comics gang ♪

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:28.494
♪ So give it up
Captain Boomerang ♪

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.029
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.331
-Grab a seat, buddy.
Looking good!

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.400
Jai, welcome.
Welcome to the show!

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.436
-Thank you, very much.
-You're looking very sharp.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.838
-Thank you.
-Also, I like the 'stache.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.273
Is that new?
-You like that?

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.640
-I love it, in fact.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.876
-Is it for a role?
-It's not necessarily.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.644
-Okay.
-I think I'm gonna

00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:48.314
hang on to it for the one
I'm about to do, but...

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.749
-Oh, really?
-I kind of --

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.618
This came to me
during, like, deep pandemic.

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.087
You know,
when I think everyone was --

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.487
had a mullet at some point...
-Yes.

00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:57.357
-...and a big mustache.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.524
-And I don't know.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.260
I just feel like I found
my vibe, like, you know?

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.196
-Yeah, I think it works.
-I arrived finally.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.496
-I think it works for you, yeah.

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:05.631
I love it.
You guys love it?

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:09.135
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.304
-It's a bit of a slug,
as they call it, you know?

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.772
They call it a slug.
-It's a good --

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.507
But it's a good 'stache.
-It's a good slug.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.509
-Mine's a bit wispy
when I grow mine out.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.710
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah?

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.947
-And it's a little sad.
And -- just panned.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.916
Universally panned, my mustache.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.450
I grew one, and I go,
"What do you think?"

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.753
and everyone just said, "No."
-No one likes it. No.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:30.457
-They didn't even say like --
"Give it a break or --"

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.824
-Some people
just can't pull it off.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.893
-No.
-My dad had one in like

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.995
the '80s and '90s,
and I feel like

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.464
I just look like him now, but...

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.332
-Yeah, my dad
always had a mustache.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.667
Still has one.
And I remember one year

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.835
he shaved it,
and that was traumatic day.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.870
-It's a weird thing
when someone shaves it.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.039
-It's bizarre.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.041
Me and my sister were like,
"Who are you?"

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.409
Like, "Why are you
in our house?"

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.677
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.877
He just looked like
a totally different person.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.346
-Seen parts of their face
you never seen before.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.147
-No, exactly.
He grew it right back.

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:57.317
I was like, "You can just put
a fake one on. I don't care."

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.318
-Sure.
-Go back to old dad.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.153
Now, you are --
You are from Australia,

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.189
and now you came over here
in L.A.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.658
You're working on something
in New York.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.160
Did you know any other
Australians working in L.A.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.363
when you moved to Los Angeles?

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.932
-When I moved, I didn't, no.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.734
Know quite a few now, obviously.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.202
But when I first got out,
didn't know anyone, really.

00:02:17.202 --> 00:02:20.840
I -- I got to know someone
who's now a friend.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.976
Russell Crowe you might know.
-Wow.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.410
[ Cheers and applause ]
Good mate of mine.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.644
-He's the greatest.

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:27.079
-He'd probably kill me
for telling this story.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:31.351
But when we first met
at a big, silly Hollywood party,

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:34.086
and I was very, like,
kind of intimidated,

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:35.121
because it's Russell, you know?

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.956
He kind of
has that air about him.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.691
But I -- you know,
I was a huge fan.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.892
So I thought I would say
g'day to him.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.226
And I was like,
leaned over and said,

00:02:41.226 --> 00:02:43.363
"Hey. Sorry, Russell,
I'm just a huge fan, you know?

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.564
I'd just
really love to meet you."

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.266
And he goes, "What's your name?"

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.902
And I said, "Jai,"
and he goes "Courtney."

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:52.105
And I go, "Yeah," and he goes,
"You want to smoke a joint?"

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.239
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.874
And I was like,
"[Bleep] yeah, man."

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.243
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.645
-Really?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.679
-First meeting Russell Crowe,
he's like --

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.682
-Day one.
Well, he keeps it real, Russell.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.250
And we got
to work together, actually,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.552
not long after that on a -- on a
film called "The Water Diviner"

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.955
that he directed,
which was a lot of fun and --

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.356
Big respect for him,
that's for sure.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.624
-Oh, he's the greatest.
I love Russell.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:12.692
Please tell him
I said, "What's up?"

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.759
-He's a friend of the show,
I know,

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.228
so I'm sure
he'll appreciate that.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.096
-I heard that you're also --

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.899
you're a very good cook,
especially pizza.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.267
-I wouldn't say
I'm a very good cook.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.502
I'm an all right cook.
I make some mean pizza, though.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:26.005
I do make some mean pizza.
I've got like a --

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.774
one of those, like, a wood-fire
oven in the backyard.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.910
So I've been doing a lot of that
while things were sort of down,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.244
particularly last year.

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:35.614
Keeping it quiet, slinging
a bit of pie, as they say.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.449
-Do they say that?
-I say it.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:39.318
-Yeah, you do, yeah.
But do you --

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.854
you have to put logs into this,
because I know --

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.590
-Yeah, well, it's a little one.
It's kind of portable.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.758
And so, you feed, like,
a chamber at the back

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:50.396
with, like, smaller logs.
It's not the hard-core like --

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.698
-But still, like --
-You can get away with it.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:55.168
-I got a picture that you --
This is your pizza here.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.969
This is unbelievable.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.504
That's one of my pies.
-Jai.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.838
-Yeah.
-You crushed.

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:04.042
I mean, I tried to do it, too,
and get a pizza going.

00:04:04.042 --> 00:04:05.645
Here's how mine --
-You make pizza?

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.547
-Well, I made this.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.648
-It's not bad.
-It's not bad, right?

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:10.883
It looks like --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.785
It looks like this isn't cooked
or something.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.821
-It's a little blonde.
It is a little blonde.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.823
-It's a little blonde.
Yeah, that was --

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:19.325
-Do you make your own dough?

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.493
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.961
-You don't make your own dough?
-No.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.295
Do I make my own dough?
No.

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:25.197
-You buy the dough?
-Well, I go to

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:28.100
the local pizzeria, and I go,
"Can I buy the dough from you?"

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.235
-That's fair enough.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.269
You leave it to the
professionals.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:31.704
-And the sauce.
And the --

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.305
-You should tell them
to cook it for you, as well.

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:36.675
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.978
-That's actually a good point.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.679
This looks great, bud.
Next time you come on,

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:43.082
I'd love to get a pie, man.
-Let's do it, for sure.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.651
-We'll sling some pies.
What's on this guy?

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.521
-That's, like, my specialty.
I do a little pepperoni.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.256
-Love it.
-Some chilies, and then,

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:52.491
I know this is polarizing,

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.260
but I'm a fan of pineapple
on my pizza.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.395
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.130
If you're not,
I don't want to hear it.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.832
It's fine.
I know people are split

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.967
with that [bleep] but...

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:03.435
-I would try it.
No, look, our audience --

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:04.803
-It's good.
-It is good.

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:05.904
-It is good.
-All right, next time,

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:07.707
we're having a taste test.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.475
"Suicide Squad."
Congrats on this.

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.310
-Thanks, man.
-This is the second time...

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.479
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.881
...that you're playing
Captain Boomerang.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.616
-That's right.
-That is a fantastic name.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:19.052
-Isn't it a great name?

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.286
-That's who I would want to play
if I'm in "The Suicide Squad."

00:05:21.286 --> 00:05:22.822
I go, "Who's playing
Captain Boomerang?"

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.291
-Yeah, Captain Boomerang.
-Yeah, and a lot of people

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:29.161
online have been really
stomping for a spinoff.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:31.264
They want to know the origin --
-So am I.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.898
I mean, let's do it.
Get on with it.

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:34.700
Let's go.
Give the people what they want.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.903
-Give the people a stand-alone
Captain Boomerang movie.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:41.307
-Absolutely.
-You would be up for that?

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.042
-Listen, I have a saying,
and it's that

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.210
a boomerang always comes back.
-Wow.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:48.481
-So, I think there's
opportunities galore with him.

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.649
We can do all of it --
TV series, spinoff,

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:53.753
whatever you want.
Pop up in "The Flash."

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.221
-You're down.
-Warner Bros. are out there.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.022
They know what's up.
-They know what's going on.

00:05:57.022 --> 00:05:58.224
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:01.226
Here's Jai Courtney
in "The Suicide Squad."

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:02.728
Take a look at this.

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.697
-[ Coughing ]

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.233
-Yo, is this a dog?
-What?

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.835
-I-Is this thing a dog?

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:11.537
-A -- A dog?
-Yes.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.772
-What -- What kind of dog
do you think it is, mate?

00:06:13.772 --> 00:06:15.942
-I don't know. I'm not familiar
with all the breeds.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:18.044
-Oh, my God!
Is it a werewolf?

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:20.079
I wanted to meet
a werewolf forever!

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.880
-Yo, they strapped me
next to a werewolf?!

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.016
Yo, let me out!
I do not do werewolves!

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.552
[ Laughter ]
-Hey, hey, he's not a werewolf!

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.253
Okay?
He's a weasel. He's harmless.

00:06:28.253 --> 00:06:30.690
I mean, he's not harmless.
He's killed 27 children.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:34.293
But, you know, we got him to --
I think he's agreed to do this.

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:37.263
Whatever the case, just everyone
get into position to drop.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.631
♪♪

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:40.132
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:42.535
-Jai Courtney, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:45.137
Captain Boomerang!

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:46.972
Check out "The Suicide Squad."

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.409
It's in theaters
and streaming on HBO Max.

